nal answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nIn trapezoid $ABCD$, $\\overline{AB}$ is parallel to $\\overline{CD}$, $AB = 7$ units, and $CD = 10$ units. Segment $EF$ is drawn parallel to $\\overline{AB}$ with $E$ lying on $\\overline{AD}$ and $F$ lying on $\\overline{BC}$. If $BF:FC = 3:4$, what is $EF$? Express your answer as a common fraction.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"e8769b7bbc476da1e46af83872a4cd540b9d77fc763c79661d2dd4d1fbc75f47"},"seconds":25.39201784133911,"seed":782921563929333086,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem, we will use the properties of similar triangles and the concept of ratios in similar figures.\n\nFirst, observe that since \\( \\overline{AB} \\parallel \\overline{CD} \\) and \\( \\overline{EF} \\parallel \\overline{AB} \\), the triangles \\( \\triangle ABE \\) and \\( \\triangle ACD \\) are similar, as are the triangles \\( \\triangle BCF \\) and \\( \\triangle BDA \\). The same applies to \\( \\triangle EFD \\) and \\( \\triangle ACD \\).\n\nGiven that \\( BF:FC = 3:4 \\), we can denote the length of \\( BF \\) as \\( 3x \\) and the length of \\( FC \\) as \\( 4x \\). Therefore, the length of \\( BC \\) is \\( 3x + 4x = 7x \\).\n\nSince \\( \\overline{EF} \\parallel \\overline{CD} \\), the triangles \\( \\triangle BEF \\) and \\( \\triangle BCD \\) are similar by AA similarity (both having a pair of corresponding angles equal due to parallel lines and the common angle at \\( B \\)). The ratio of the corresponding sides of these similar triangles is equal to the ratio of \\( BF \\) to \\( BC \\), which is \\( \\frac{3x}{7x} = \\frac{3}{7} \\).\n\nThis ratio also applies to the lengths of \\( EF \\) and \\( CD \\). Therefore, we have:\n\\[\n\\frac{EF}{CD} = \\frac{3}{7}\n\\]\nSince \\( CD = 10 \\) units, we can substitute this value into the equation:\n\\[\nEF = \\frac{3}{7} \\times 10 = \\frac{30}{7}\n\\]\nThus, the length of \\( EF \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{30}{7}}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\frac{30}{7}}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
